__pycache__/
*.pyc
node_modules/
dist/
.DS_Store

# Rendered sprite output IS committed, for now. ART_PIPELINE.md §9 wants CI
# to regenerate it from art/src/*.blend, but the .blend sources are too large
# for git (see below) so CI has nothing to render from -- and without the PNGs
# the deployed build falls back to procedural shapes. They are small (~3 MB),
# and tools/quantize_sprites.py keeps them passing the art gate. Revisit when
# sources move to LFS and the rig runs in CI.

# Blender sources: mostly NOT in git, but the blanket rule was overstated.
# The tank files genuinely cannot be tracked -- tiger_tank_clean is 404 MB and
# Tiger_Tank_Rig 240 MB, past GitHub's 100 MB hard limit. But the vehicles added
# since are 7-52 MB, and building shells are smaller still, so "hundreds of MB"
# was never true of them.
#
# ART_PIPELINE.md §8 requires sources to accompany contributed art, and CLAUDE.md
# forbids committing rendered sprites without their .blend. Nothing has satisfied
# that yet. Building sources are small enough to satisfy it in plain git, without
# waiting on Git LFS (#28), so art/src/buildings/ is tracked.
#
# Vehicle and character sources stay out for now: several are over the hard
# limit, and mixing tracked and untracked siblings by size would be arbitrary.
# Their provenance travels in each render script's CREDIT string and the credit
# field of every manifest.
art/src/*.blend
art/src/*.blend1
!art/src/buildings/
!art/src/buildings/*.blend
# Blender auto-backups: never wanted, anywhere.
*.blend1

# Brainstorming companion scratch (superpowers) — never committed.
.superpowers/
